1
00:01:40,640 --> 00:01:42,280
I asked the guys at the motor pool.

2
00:01:42,439 --> 00:01:43,599
They checked it over.

3
00:01:43,599 --> 00:01:45,280
Said the engine isn't leaking oil,

4
00:01:45,280 --> 00:01:46,519
and the wiring is fine too.

5
00:01:46,560 --> 00:01:48,280
The oil and filter were both changed.

6
00:01:48,280 --> 00:01:50,079
They haven't found any specific issues for now.

7
00:01:50,079 --> 00:01:51,200
Avoid shifting gears too frequently,

8
00:01:51,200 --> 00:01:53,040
and don't press the clutch too hard.

9
00:01:53,040 --> 00:01:54,519
Avoid sudden acceleration or braking.

10
00:01:54,519 --> 00:01:55,519
At the intersection we just passed,

11
00:01:55,519 --> 00:01:56,760
there's a specialized hospital to the southwest.

12
00:01:56,760 --> 00:01:58,200
Is it dermatology or maternity?

13
00:01:59,760 --> 00:02:01,319
It was too far to see clearly.

14
00:02:01,400 --> 00:02:02,920
Is there a problem with that hospital?

15
00:02:03,719 --> 00:02:04,400
If necessary,

16
00:02:04,400 --> 00:02:05,280
I can go back and check right now.

17
00:02:05,280 --> 00:02:06,000
If you can't remember a hospital,

18
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:07,400
you can go back and look again.

19
00:02:07,680 --> 00:02:08,719
But if you can't remember a conversation?

20
00:02:08,879 --> 00:02:10,319
Will you ask them to repeat it?

21
00:02:13,319 --> 00:02:14,759
From now on, the people I meet,

22
00:02:14,759 --> 00:02:15,520
the words they say,

23
00:02:15,520 --> 00:02:16,199
everything I need to remember,

24
00:02:16,199 --> 00:02:17,080
I will remember it all.

25
00:02:17,080 --> 00:02:18,479
You definitely won't remember.

26
00:02:18,479 --> 00:02:19,599
Who do you think you are?

27
00:02:19,719 --> 00:02:21,560
Three lines from one person is hard enough.

28
00:02:21,680 --> 00:02:22,599
What about ten people?

29
00:02:22,599 --> 00:02:23,520
Sometimes at a dinner,

30
00:02:23,520 --> 00:02:24,400
there are over a dozen strangers.

31
00:02:24,400 --> 00:02:25,680
What they say is half-true, half-false.

32
00:02:25,680 --> 00:02:26,639
Which line has a double meaning,

33
00:02:26,639 --> 00:02:27,520
which sentence has a hidden meaning...

34
00:02:27,520 --> 00:02:28,759
You won't even understand it when you hear it.

35
00:02:28,759 --> 00:02:29,319
How will you remember?

36
00:02:31,400 --> 00:02:34,680
I heard some have naturally good memory.

37
00:02:35,560 --> 00:02:36,960
I really don't have that talent.

38
00:02:37,159 --> 00:02:38,120
But I want to try.

39
00:02:38,120 --> 00:02:40,319
I don't know how to remember everything,

40
00:02:40,319 --> 00:02:41,719
but there must be a trick to it, right?

41
00:02:41,719 --> 00:02:42,719
Force yourself.

42
00:02:42,919 --> 00:02:43,960
The brain is like a stomach.

43
00:02:43,960 --> 00:02:45,680
If you can't eat, force it down.

44
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:47,000
Sooner or later, you'll stretch it out.

45
00:02:47,280 --> 00:02:48,680
Lao Wei asked me to grade you all.

46
00:02:48,919 --> 00:02:49,759
For me, it's very simple.

47
00:02:49,800 --> 00:02:50,599
Just this one thing.

48
00:02:50,599 --> 00:02:51,520
If you can remember, you stay.

49
00:02:51,520 --> 00:02:52,800
If you can't, I'm sending you back.

50
00:02:57,520 --> 00:02:58,680
What are you thinking about?

51
00:02:58,919 --> 00:02:59,759
Cursing me in your head?

52
00:03:00,639 --> 00:03:02,080
I'm memorizing what you just said.

53
00:03:04,599 --> 00:03:05,599
From now on,

54
00:03:06,080 --> 00:03:07,039
every person you meet,

55
00:03:07,039 --> 00:03:07,919
every word they say,

56
00:03:07,919 --> 00:03:08,919
every office you enter,

57
00:03:08,919 --> 00:03:09,599
every restaurant,

58
00:03:09,599 --> 00:03:10,400
every shop.

59
00:03:10,400 --> 00:03:11,080
Whether the people you meet

60
00:03:11,080 --> 00:03:12,520
are on the street or at home,

61
00:03:12,520 --> 00:03:13,479
in a teahouse or a dance hall,

62
00:03:13,479 --> 00:03:14,680
no matter how noisy the setting is,

63
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:15,319
you will remember everything.

64
00:03:15,319 --> 00:03:16,360
Every day before getting off work,

65
00:03:16,360 --> 00:03:17,280
whether it's at seven,

66
00:03:17,280 --> 00:03:18,439
or at twelve,

67
00:03:18,439 --> 00:03:20,199
you will recite to me what they said.

68
00:03:20,439 --> 00:03:21,840
You can't forget it even after reciting.

69
00:03:21,840 --> 00:03:23,120
Don't even think about fooling me.

70
00:03:23,719 --> 00:03:24,800
If I catch you once,

71
00:03:25,159 --> 00:03:26,120
you're out.

72
00:04:49,879 --> 00:04:50,720
My uncle...

73
00:04:50,720 --> 00:04:51,680
he really does live in here.

74
00:04:52,000 --> 00:04:54,360
He lives right inside, Building 3, Unit 2,

75
00:04:54,600 --> 00:04:55,519
Room 101.

76
00:04:55,920 --> 00:04:57,000
Room 101, right?

77
00:04:57,519 --> 00:04:58,959
Then sign in here.

78
00:04:59,240 --> 00:04:59,879
Brother Qi.

79
00:05:00,839 --> 00:05:01,600
Done.

80
00:05:04,720 --> 00:05:06,160
I can't believe you bluffed your way in.

81
00:05:06,639 --> 00:05:07,759
What did you tell them this time?

82
00:05:07,959 --> 00:05:09,639
I said my aunt and uncle both live here,

83
00:05:09,639 --> 00:05:10,600
and I came to see them.

84
00:05:11,279 --> 00:05:12,360
Lies just roll off your tongue.

85
00:05:12,560 --> 00:05:13,800
Didn't they ask for their names,

86
00:05:13,800 --> 00:05:14,879
or which room they're in?

87
00:05:14,920 --> 00:05:15,519
They did.

88
00:05:15,920 --> 00:05:16,800
What did you say?

89
00:05:17,079 --> 00:05:18,279
I told the truth.

90
00:05:18,399 --> 00:05:20,000
Because my aunt and uncle really live here.

91
00:05:23,399 --> 00:05:24,279
Ever since you were little,

92
00:05:24,319 --> 00:05:25,639
you've always been this...

93
00:05:25,800 --> 00:05:26,480
serious.

94
00:07:22,519 --> 00:07:23,519
What are you doing here?

95
00:07:24,519 --> 00:07:25,560
My uncle lives around here.

96
00:07:25,560 --> 00:07:26,560
Just came to visit.

97
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:27,040
What about you?

98
00:07:27,040 --> 00:07:27,839
Uncle?

99
00:07:28,680 --> 00:07:31,399
I thought Old Wu was your brother-in-law?

100
00:07:31,519 --> 00:07:32,560
Does he live around here too?

101
00:07:32,720 --> 00:07:33,519
No.

102
00:07:34,639 --> 00:07:36,480
I figured it's all family anyway.

103
00:07:36,480 --> 00:07:37,279
And you?

104
00:07:37,279 --> 00:07:38,199
I'm here to find someone.

105
00:07:38,639 --> 00:07:39,600
Your brother-in-law.

106
00:07:39,839 --> 00:07:41,360
He insisted on showing me some textile mill.

107
00:07:41,600 --> 00:07:43,160
It's about to go out of business.

108
00:07:43,399 --> 00:07:44,519
Acting like they have strict rules.

109
00:07:44,959 --> 00:07:46,720
They blocked the gate with a steel plate.

110
00:07:46,839 --> 00:07:47,439
I had to take a crap.

111
00:07:47,439 --> 00:07:48,600
Almost shit my pants.

112
00:07:49,560 --> 00:07:50,720
Do you know what I used to wipe?

113
00:07:55,279 --> 00:07:56,160
I've done that too.

114
00:07:56,160 --> 00:07:57,680
I've even used stones and leaves.

115
00:07:58,000 --> 00:07:59,759
None of those beat a wall corner!

116
00:08:01,680 --> 00:08:02,319
Right.

117
00:08:02,519 --> 00:08:03,279
Where's my brother-in-law?

118
00:08:03,279 --> 00:08:04,040
Where is he?

119
00:08:06,240 --> 00:08:06,839
Let's go.

120
00:08:09,240 --> 00:08:11,879
"Amazing Tales" says the truth can't be faked.

121
00:08:12,199 --> 00:08:13,399
If you tell a lie,

122
00:08:13,560 --> 00:08:15,360
you have to find someone to cover it up.

123
00:08:15,480 --> 00:08:17,879
As long as he's real, you won't be exposed.

124
00:08:18,759 --> 00:08:19,680
Where's my brother-in-law?

125
00:08:20,000 --> 00:08:20,800
Where is he?

126
00:08:22,040 --> 00:08:23,120
He was just here.

127
00:08:25,079 --> 00:08:26,000
Give me a ride! Give me a ride!

128
00:08:26,160 --> 00:08:26,319
Okay.

129
00:08:26,560 --> 00:08:27,079
Where to?

130
00:08:28,399 --> 00:08:29,079
Boss Lin.

131
00:08:29,480 --> 00:08:30,160
Old Wu.

132
00:08:30,720 --> 00:08:31,199
Old Wu.

133
00:08:32,600 --> 00:08:33,440
You're not up yet?

134
00:08:35,360 --> 00:08:37,799
Can we see that textile mill you mentioned?

135
00:08:37,799 --> 00:08:38,519
I happen to be free right now.

136
00:08:38,519 --> 00:08:39,200
Are you free?

137
00:08:40,639 --> 00:08:41,559
Okay, okay, okay.

138
00:08:42,759 --> 00:08:43,360
I'm hanging up.

139
00:08:45,279 --> 00:08:46,600
The cops are here! The cops are here!

140
00:08:47,159 --> 00:08:48,240
Where did he go?

141
00:08:51,080 --> 00:08:52,320
We'll get back to work then.

142
00:08:52,960 --> 00:08:54,039
Hurry up, I'm in a rush.

143
00:08:54,080 --> 00:08:54,799
Hurry, hurry, hurry!

144
00:09:48,519 --> 00:09:50,639
1729

145
00:09:52,679 --> 00:09:55,120
5722

146
00:10:02,879 --> 00:10:03,679
Where did they go?

147
00:10:03,759 --> 00:10:04,679
Come with me to the post office.

148
00:10:07,720 --> 00:10:09,080
Hurry up and fix your car.

149
00:10:09,080 --> 00:10:10,159
Make sure you don't block the road.

150
00:10:13,320 --> 00:10:14,159
What's their problem?

151
00:10:14,639 --> 00:10:15,200
Stop the car!

152
00:10:15,679 --> 00:10:16,240
Stop the car!

153
00:10:16,360 --> 00:10:17,159
Watch out!

154
00:10:17,639 --> 00:10:18,240
Stop the car!

155
00:10:30,519 --> 00:10:31,279
If we rush the arrest,

156
00:10:31,279 --> 00:10:32,279
Aren't we going straight in?

157
00:10:32,879 --> 00:10:33,720
it would alert the target.

158
00:10:34,159 --> 00:10:35,559
Are you going to tip him off?

159
00:10:37,360 --> 00:10:38,600
Find the number for the security section.

160
00:10:38,600 --> 00:10:39,600
Hand it to me when it connects.

161
00:10:45,320 --> 00:10:45,679
Hello.

162
00:10:45,679 --> 00:10:47,120
Please transfer me to the security section.

163
00:10:49,879 --> 00:10:50,600
Who's calling?

164
00:10:50,600 --> 00:10:52,200
Hello, Minzhong State Security Bureau.

165
00:10:52,200 --> 00:10:53,279
We'd like to ask Fan Chen a few questions.

166
00:10:55,039 --> 00:10:55,759
Speaking.

167
00:10:56,080 --> 00:10:56,720
What's this about?

168
00:10:56,720 --> 00:10:57,279
Sorry.

169
00:10:57,480 --> 00:10:58,679
The person we're looking for is a woman.

170
00:10:58,879 --> 00:11:00,200
She probably has the same name as you.

171
00:11:10,279 --> 00:11:10,720
Who is it?

172
00:11:10,720 --> 00:11:11,279
Who called?

173
00:11:11,600 --> 00:11:12,440
The sorting room.

174
00:11:13,519 --> 00:11:14,320
Gotta finish sorting the parcels.

175
00:11:14,559 --> 00:11:15,759
Telling me to get back to work.

176
00:11:16,000 --> 00:11:16,840
We just ran out of water.

177
00:11:17,279 --> 00:11:18,120
The bosses want tea,

178
00:11:18,279 --> 00:11:19,080
so I'm running errands.

179
00:11:19,440 --> 00:11:20,200
Must be tough.

180
00:11:20,320 --> 00:11:21,360
That's life.

181
00:11:21,559 --> 00:11:22,440
Here you go.

182
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:24,519
Here you go.

183
00:11:31,039 --> 00:11:33,000
Hi, where's the Security Section?

184
00:11:33,039 --> 00:11:33,840
Can I help you?

185
00:11:35,399 --> 00:11:36,240
Police business.

186
00:11:36,240 --> 00:11:37,120
It's right here.

187
00:11:41,879 --> 00:11:42,679
Lao Fan.

188
00:11:44,240 --> 00:11:44,720
Lao Fan!

189
00:11:45,440 --> 00:11:46,279
Who are you looking for?

190
00:11:47,279 --> 00:11:48,320
I'm Lao Fan's friend.

191
00:11:48,440 --> 00:11:49,639
He told me to meet him in this room.

192
00:11:49,639 --> 00:11:50,240
Where is he?

193
00:11:50,440 --> 00:11:51,600
He just went to get hot water.

194
00:11:52,440 --> 00:11:53,240
Where's the hot water room?

195
00:11:53,639 --> 00:11:54,639
Go through the sorting room,

196
00:11:54,679 --> 00:11:55,519
and it's downstairs.

197
00:12:05,360 --> 00:12:06,200
What are you doing?

198
00:14:06,360 --> 00:14:07,159
Are you crazy?!

199
00:14:07,240 --> 00:14:07,919
Watch where you're going!

200
00:14:21,200 --> 00:14:21,679
Cuff him.

201
00:14:25,480 --> 00:14:25,960
Get up.

202
00:14:38,399 --> 00:14:39,320
What were you thinking?

203
00:14:39,759 --> 00:14:40,720
Showing your hand right from the start.

204
00:14:40,720 --> 00:14:41,519
Who taught you that?

205
00:14:41,679 --> 00:14:42,600
Sorry, Brother Qi.

206
00:14:42,799 --> 00:14:45,000
I didn't expect him to be in the security section.

207
00:14:45,320 --> 00:14:46,120
I'll definitely remember this.

208
00:14:46,200 --> 00:14:46,639
And take it as a lesson.

209
00:14:46,639 --> 00:14:47,320
Remember my ass.

210
00:14:47,360 --> 00:14:48,399
Do you even need to memorize that?

211
00:14:48,399 --> 00:14:49,960
Your brain just doesn't know how to pivot.

212
00:14:51,519 --> 00:14:53,360
I'll try to pivot more from now on.

213
00:15:02,960 --> 00:15:03,799
What the hell is wrong with you!

214
00:15:03,799 --> 00:15:04,320
No, no.

215
00:15:04,559 --> 00:15:06,000
The car in front slammed on the brakes.

216
00:15:09,759 --> 00:15:10,240
Brother Qi.

217
00:15:10,360 --> 00:15:10,799
Maybe we should just let it go.

218
00:15:11,159 --> 00:15:12,919
We still have to interrogate that postman.

219
00:15:13,279 --> 00:15:13,879
Brother Qi!

220
00:15:14,240 --> 00:15:14,600
Look.

221
00:15:14,600 --> 00:15:15,600
Brother Qi, just let it go.

222
00:15:17,679 --> 00:15:18,200
This has nothing to do with you.

223
00:15:18,240 --> 00:15:19,559
Please wait here for a second.

224
00:15:20,559 --> 00:15:21,039
Just a moment.

225
00:15:21,320 --> 00:15:22,039
Kill the engine.

226
00:15:22,600 --> 00:15:23,279
Stop the car!

227
00:15:23,759 --> 00:15:24,240
Stop the car!

228
00:15:37,320 --> 00:15:38,000
Hello.

229
00:15:38,159 --> 00:15:39,679
Please show your ID and driver's license.

230
00:15:39,799 --> 00:15:40,559
And vehicle registration.

231
00:15:41,159 --> 00:15:42,799
I was in a rush today and forgot them.

232
00:15:49,960 --> 00:15:50,600
Let's go, move.

233
00:15:51,279 --> 00:15:52,000
Take this seriously.

234
00:15:52,600 --> 00:15:53,440
Driver, you're looking at

235
00:15:54,679 --> 00:15:55,519
driving without a license,

236
00:15:55,519 --> 00:15:56,519
reckless driving,

237
00:15:56,639 --> 00:15:57,559
and no vehicle registration.

238
00:15:58,039 --> 00:15:59,120
Frankly, you're in big trouble.

239
00:15:59,120 --> 00:15:59,519
Hold on.

240
00:15:59,519 --> 00:16:01,240
Where's the accomplice in the passenger seat?

241
00:16:01,240 --> 00:16:01,679
Officer,

242
00:16:01,679 --> 00:16:02,840
I really have urgent business.

243
00:16:02,879 --> 00:16:03,559
You have to let me go.

244
00:16:03,600 --> 00:16:04,879
Otherwise, you'll be in big trouble.

245
00:16:12,639 --> 00:16:13,440
Let's go.

246
00:16:20,679 --> 00:16:21,480
Fine, let's go.

247
00:16:22,440 --> 00:16:23,000
Move, move, move.

248
00:16:41,799 --> 00:16:43,080
I was just busy.

249
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:45,840
An oxcart rear-ended a bicycle.

250
00:16:45,840 --> 00:16:46,919
Awaiting orders, Captain.

251
00:16:48,440 --> 00:16:49,519
Right, right.

252
00:16:49,679 --> 00:16:50,840
Which department?

253
00:16:53,360 --> 00:16:54,039
Is that so?

254
00:16:55,519 --> 00:16:57,080
Well, they didn't mention that.

255
00:16:57,559 --> 00:16:59,039
Understood. We'll definitely cooperate.

256
00:17:00,039 --> 00:17:00,799
Let them through immediately.

257
00:17:13,839 --> 00:17:15,200
What do these numbers mean?

258
00:17:15,359 --> 00:17:16,720
I don't know.

259
00:17:16,720 --> 00:17:18,240
I'm just a courier.

260
00:17:18,400 --> 00:17:20,000
I only deliver messages.

261
00:17:20,559 --> 00:17:21,799
Such a small piece of paper.

262
00:17:21,839 --> 00:17:22,720
You didn't keep it at home,

263
00:17:22,720 --> 00:17:24,039
but insisted on hiding it here.

264
00:17:24,160 --> 00:17:24,920
Doesn't your tooth hurt?

265
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:26,720
I know this is very important,

266
00:17:26,960 --> 00:17:28,079
but who it's for,

267
00:17:28,359 --> 00:17:29,279
I have no idea.

268
00:17:30,000 --> 00:17:31,279
You can check if you don't believe me.

269
00:17:31,599 --> 00:17:33,119
These are the rules.

270
00:17:34,039 --> 00:17:35,720
If you were my superior,

271
00:17:36,319 --> 00:17:37,440
would you let me know?

272
00:17:42,359 --> 00:17:43,240
What is it?

273
00:17:52,640 --> 00:17:53,440
You're not going up, right?

274
00:17:56,960 --> 00:17:57,519
All right.

275
00:17:57,519 --> 00:17:58,680
He's finally back.

276
00:17:59,039 --> 00:17:59,720
Where's the car?

277
00:18:02,079 --> 00:18:02,960
I drove it back.

278
00:18:03,359 --> 00:18:04,440
It's parked in the yard.

279
00:18:04,880 --> 00:18:05,960
How did you get through?

280
00:18:06,160 --> 00:18:07,319
Tell us all about it,

281
00:18:07,480 --> 00:18:08,960
so we can learn a thing or two.

282
00:18:09,200 --> 00:18:10,680
According to the Traffic Penalty Regulations,

283
00:18:10,799 --> 00:18:12,799
directing traffic for 80 minutes is enough.

284
00:18:13,200 --> 00:18:14,039
The traffic police said so.

285
00:18:14,559 --> 00:18:16,559
There's no such rule in the regulations.

286
00:18:17,880 --> 00:18:18,519
I'm positive.

287
00:18:18,640 --> 00:18:19,839
If he says there is, there is.

288
00:18:19,839 --> 00:18:20,960
It's the same for rule breakers.

289
00:18:21,079 --> 00:18:23,000
But when the time was up, he wasn't there.

290
00:18:23,000 --> 00:18:24,279
So I just drove the car back myself.

291
00:18:25,720 --> 00:18:26,680
How about that postman?

292
00:18:26,680 --> 00:18:27,279
Did he confess?

293
00:18:31,160 --> 00:18:32,960
Comrades, let's pack up.

294
00:18:34,119 --> 00:18:35,240
Once Old Wei comes back,

295
00:18:35,240 --> 00:18:36,799
we'll search Fan Chen's home and office.

296
00:18:36,920 --> 00:18:37,400
He confessed.

297
00:18:39,200 --> 00:18:40,359
Why don't you go ask him?

298
00:18:49,759 --> 00:18:51,119
His hometown is Shishi.

299
00:18:51,319 --> 00:18:52,599
He went to Taiwan, China when he was young.

300
00:18:52,920 --> 00:18:54,079
He's a good photographer.

301
00:18:54,279 --> 00:18:55,680
He accidentally killed someone.

302
00:18:55,920 --> 00:18:57,319
They got him out of prison

303
00:18:57,559 --> 00:18:59,039
and into the "Military Intelligence Bureau".

304
00:18:59,359 --> 00:19:01,000
He initially worked at a state photo studio.

305
00:19:01,400 --> 00:19:02,799
Later he was transferred to the post office,

306
00:19:03,039 --> 00:19:03,839
where he's worked until now.

307
00:19:05,319 --> 00:19:07,519
Who are these codes for?

308
00:19:09,079 --> 00:19:10,160
Do we have a rough idea?

309
00:19:10,480 --> 00:19:11,200
He's right.

310
00:19:11,400 --> 00:19:13,119
If I were his boss, I wouldn't tell him either.

311
00:19:13,680 --> 00:19:14,799
But this guy is smart.

312
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:16,000
From the clues,

313
00:19:16,599 --> 00:19:17,519
he has a guess.

314
00:19:18,039 --> 00:19:19,400
Yesterday at 3:10 PM,

315
00:19:19,519 --> 00:19:21,160
he put this code and a gold bar

316
00:19:21,200 --> 00:19:22,359
next to Taijiang Department Store,

317
00:19:22,440 --> 00:19:23,720
in an abandoned mailbox.

318
00:19:24,160 --> 00:19:25,200
According to the original plan,

319
00:19:25,559 --> 00:19:27,400
someone was to pick it up within ten minutes.

320
00:19:28,200 --> 00:19:29,880
Next to Taijiang Department Store

321
00:19:30,000 --> 00:19:31,200
is Institute 761.

322
00:19:31,920 --> 00:19:32,920
Regarding the missiles...

323
00:19:33,480 --> 00:19:34,440
We have a thief on our hands.

324
00:19:34,880 --> 00:19:36,200
But the other party didn't pick it up.

325
00:19:36,640 --> 00:19:38,519
This mailbox has been scrapped since then,

326
00:19:38,799 --> 00:19:39,880
and won't be used again.

327
00:19:40,680 --> 00:19:41,720
If they don't take it today,

328
00:19:42,720 --> 00:19:43,359
what about tomorrow?

329
00:19:44,000 --> 00:19:44,680
Or the day after?

330
00:19:44,920 --> 00:19:46,960
Institute 761 holds the key to the missiles.

331
00:19:46,960 --> 00:19:48,279
The enemy is practically drooling over it.

332
00:19:48,400 --> 00:19:50,279
Out of thousands of people at Institute 761,

333
00:19:50,759 --> 00:19:53,240
a wavering traitor is hiding among them.

334
00:19:54,640 --> 00:19:55,720
Who could it be?

335
00:19:57,400 --> 00:19:59,400
What cards are the Communists going to play?

336
00:19:59,400 --> 00:20:00,200
How will they play them?

337
00:20:00,359 --> 00:20:02,039
You have to show me the cards, Old Zheng.

338
00:20:02,279 --> 00:20:03,440
With intelligence,

339
00:20:03,440 --> 00:20:04,359
you can't just wait.

340
00:20:04,359 --> 00:20:05,640
You have to go out and grab it.

341
00:20:05,880 --> 00:20:07,200
What about the missile progress?

342
00:20:07,200 --> 00:20:07,960
Answer me!

343
00:20:17,680 --> 00:20:18,599
I didn't eat much for lunch.

344
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:19,720
I can't hold on much longer.

345
00:20:20,640 --> 00:20:21,920
I'll go buy some water for everyone.

346
00:20:22,039 --> 00:20:23,480
Please get me eight bottles of soda,

347
00:20:24,000 --> 00:20:24,599
boss.

348
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:47,200
Take care, sir.

349
00:20:47,920 --> 00:20:50,079
We look forward to your next visit.

350
00:20:57,079 --> 00:20:57,920
The missile intel-

351
00:20:58,359 --> 00:20:59,400
You scared me to death!

352
00:20:59,400 --> 00:21:01,319
I thought it was the Communists.

353
00:21:01,319 --> 00:21:03,519
There might be an issue with the missile intel.

354
00:21:05,400 --> 00:21:06,640
My mole in the mainland's State Security

355
00:21:06,640 --> 00:21:07,599
sent a message saying

356
00:21:08,200 --> 00:21:09,640
Professor Cao's courier was caught.

357
00:21:11,680 --> 00:21:12,759
He hasn't met the professor,

358
00:21:13,359 --> 00:21:14,440
and doesn't know any information.

359
00:21:14,440 --> 00:21:16,039
Even if he breaks and talks,

360
00:21:16,119 --> 00:21:17,839
the mainland won't learn our secrets.

361
00:21:17,839 --> 00:21:19,880
Plus, the latest handover wasn't completed.

362
00:21:19,880 --> 00:21:21,000
This actually works in our favor.

363
00:21:21,119 --> 00:21:23,680
Are you delivering good news or bad news?

364
00:21:23,799 --> 00:21:24,880
Or a mix of both?

365
00:21:26,480 --> 00:21:27,640
It happened suddenly.

366
00:21:28,240 --> 00:21:28,920
If by any chance

367
00:21:28,920 --> 00:21:31,240
we don't get the Institute 761 intel on time...

368
00:21:32,000 --> 00:21:33,279
You mean to say,

369
00:21:34,039 --> 00:21:35,799
you want me to come up with a plan for you?

370
00:21:39,279 --> 00:21:40,119
I heard

371
00:21:40,599 --> 00:21:42,400
you're meeting the higher-ups tomorrow.

372
00:21:43,240 --> 00:21:44,640
I rushed here to brief you,

373
00:21:44,640 --> 00:21:45,519
so you wouldn't be

374
00:21:45,759 --> 00:21:46,640
put on the defensive.

375
00:21:46,680 --> 00:21:48,119
I'm already on the defensive.

376
00:21:48,720 --> 00:21:50,279
Confucius said, "If a man lacks trust,

377
00:21:50,279 --> 00:21:51,480
I know not what he can accomplish."

378
00:21:52,039 --> 00:21:53,279
Last time you said

379
00:21:53,279 --> 00:21:54,440
there'd be no problem.

380
00:21:55,039 --> 00:21:56,119
With tomorrow's meeting,

381
00:21:56,359 --> 00:21:57,400
I don't even dare to go.

382
00:21:58,079 --> 00:21:59,480
You go to the meeting in my place.

383
00:22:22,240 --> 00:22:23,400
If there's no main dish,

384
00:22:24,039 --> 00:22:25,839
just pile the side dishes high.

385
00:22:26,759 --> 00:22:28,640
Do we have the map of the naval pier?

386
00:22:29,200 --> 00:22:31,599
Is the military exercise intel accurate?

387
00:22:31,759 --> 00:22:33,359
Don't you have a lot of informants?

388
00:22:33,640 --> 00:22:34,839
If we have nothing at all,

389
00:22:34,920 --> 00:22:36,359
we might as well pack it in early

390
00:22:36,559 --> 00:22:37,680
and go home to farm.

391
00:22:38,640 --> 00:22:39,279
Let's go.

392
00:22:48,680 --> 00:22:49,160
Brother Qi.

393
00:22:53,839 --> 00:22:55,720
Hello, Minzhong State Security Bureau.

394
00:22:55,720 --> 00:22:57,359
We'd like to ask Fan Chen a few questions.

395
00:22:58,480 --> 00:22:59,319
Where did you go?

396
00:22:59,359 --> 00:23:00,160
Come with me to the post office.

397
00:23:15,039 --> 00:23:16,160
Have you read this book?

398
00:23:19,039 --> 00:23:19,519
I've heard of it.

399
00:23:19,799 --> 00:23:20,920
Haven't read it yet.

400
00:23:22,759 --> 00:23:23,720
Do you like reading?

401
00:23:24,359 --> 00:23:25,279
I like Jin Yong.

402
00:23:26,240 --> 00:23:27,359
You said you've seen this man.

403
00:23:27,480 --> 00:23:27,920
When?

404
00:23:27,920 --> 00:23:28,759
Where?

405
00:23:29,759 --> 00:23:30,960
Before I attended the training class.

406
00:23:31,279 --> 00:23:32,519
He delivered a parcel to me.

407
00:23:32,640 --> 00:23:33,720
You were home?

408
00:23:35,000 --> 00:23:36,440
No. 02, Lane 75.

409
00:23:36,920 --> 00:23:37,519
He came three times.

410
00:23:37,519 --> 00:23:38,480
No one was home.

411
00:23:38,799 --> 00:23:40,839
So I came to catch you right when I got to work.

412
00:23:42,079 --> 00:23:42,880
What a coincidence.

413
00:23:43,680 --> 00:23:45,079
That's my newly rented place.

414
00:23:45,319 --> 00:23:45,960
According to him,

415
00:23:46,359 --> 00:23:47,640
the letters and telegrams in that area

416
00:23:47,640 --> 00:23:48,599
are all delivered by him.

417
00:23:48,759 --> 00:23:49,400
Right, Brother Qi.

418
00:23:50,279 --> 00:23:51,680
How did you know

419
00:23:51,680 --> 00:23:53,960
he'd come out the back door of those houses?

420
00:23:53,960 --> 00:23:55,039
Why didn't you chase him when he ran?

421
00:23:56,519 --> 00:23:58,319
It happened so fast.

422
00:23:58,319 --> 00:23:59,559
I didn't expect him to come out.

423
00:24:00,279 --> 00:24:01,200
I didn't react in time.

424
00:24:01,799 --> 00:24:02,680
If I were the boss,

425
00:24:03,599 --> 00:24:04,559
I'd suspect you.

426
00:24:10,039 --> 00:24:10,880
What are you trying to say?

427
00:24:12,039 --> 00:24:13,160
Suspecting me for no reason.

428
00:24:13,279 --> 00:24:14,039
Suspecting our own people.

429
00:24:14,039 --> 00:24:15,440
Is that a division rule or a bureau rule?

430
00:24:15,440 --> 00:24:17,279
So you need to turn yourself into a map.

431
00:24:18,039 --> 00:24:19,400
As small as this street,

432
00:24:19,599 --> 00:24:22,000
or as big as the city, countryside, and province.

433
00:24:22,160 --> 00:24:23,839
Every alley, every intersection,

434
00:24:24,000 --> 00:24:25,400
every well, every tree,

435
00:24:25,599 --> 00:24:26,680
must be etched into your mind.

436
00:24:26,680 --> 00:24:28,079
Even if you're blindfolded,

437
00:24:28,119 --> 00:24:29,559
you should be able to cross the city.

438
00:24:33,000 --> 00:24:33,480
If I were him,

439
00:24:33,519 --> 00:24:34,559
I would've come out from there too.

440
00:24:34,880 --> 00:24:35,960
I would've taken a gamble too.

441
00:24:35,960 --> 00:24:37,160
Gambled on whether the one guarding there

442
00:24:37,200 --> 00:24:38,240
was a rookie,

443
00:24:38,240 --> 00:24:39,359
an idiot,

444
00:24:39,359 --> 00:24:40,319
or an ally.

445
00:24:46,960 --> 00:24:48,240
Never suspecting anyone in your life,

446
00:24:48,440 --> 00:24:49,279
and never being suspected,

447
00:24:49,279 --> 00:24:50,200
means you've lived in vain.

448
00:24:50,640 --> 00:24:51,759
What does it mean to be an investigator?

449
00:24:52,359 --> 00:24:53,200
In my eyes,

450
00:24:54,279 --> 00:24:55,160
Old Wei could also be

451
00:24:55,160 --> 00:24:56,359
a mole for the "Military Intelligence Bureau".

452
00:24:56,680 --> 00:24:58,279
I don't know what's inside.

453
00:25:05,799 --> 00:25:07,160
This is a box someone sent him.

454
00:25:07,759 --> 00:25:08,359
Is there a problem?

455
00:25:08,720 --> 00:25:09,759
The wooden boards are too thick.

456
00:25:09,839 --> 00:25:10,519
Light can't shine through.

457
00:25:10,519 --> 00:25:11,519
You can't see anything.

458
00:25:11,680 --> 00:25:12,680
General on Horseback.

459
00:25:12,720 --> 00:25:14,039
I haven't seen this type of lock before.

460
00:25:14,359 --> 00:25:15,200
It won't be easy to open.

461
00:25:15,920 --> 00:25:16,519
Give me a hammer.

462
00:25:26,279 --> 00:25:27,440
Here, let me take a picture first.

463
00:25:30,400 --> 00:25:30,920
Okay.

464
00:25:37,759 --> 00:25:38,920
I won't be able to put it back together.

465
00:25:39,200 --> 00:25:40,559
Won't open it just because you can't fix it?

466
00:25:41,039 --> 00:25:42,400
If you fear choking, just stop eating.

467
00:25:44,960 --> 00:25:46,200
Let the Tech Section look at it.

468
00:25:46,480 --> 00:25:47,720
Do not open it before entering the darkroom.

469
00:25:48,240 --> 00:25:48,839
Brother Qi.

470
00:25:49,000 --> 00:25:49,920
Come take a look over here.

471
00:25:56,079 --> 00:25:56,640
Brother Qi.

472
00:25:56,960 --> 00:25:57,839
How much force did it take

473
00:25:58,119 --> 00:25:58,920
to jump down from above

474
00:25:58,920 --> 00:26:00,039
and leave such a deep footprint?

475
00:26:00,200 --> 00:26:01,960
He definitely escaped out the back window.

476
00:26:03,839 --> 00:26:04,759
Before I entered the room during the day,

477
00:26:04,759 --> 00:26:05,960
someone else had also been here.

478
00:26:14,839 --> 00:26:15,519
Tenth floor.

479
00:26:19,079 --> 00:26:21,359
Early out, late in, acting all mysterious.

480
00:26:22,160 --> 00:26:22,799
You,

481
00:26:22,799 --> 00:26:24,440
what kind of business are you in exactly?

482
00:26:26,319 --> 00:26:27,519
Just running a small business.

483
00:26:27,680 --> 00:26:28,960
Socializing is inevitable.

484
00:26:29,759 --> 00:26:30,759
Young man,

485
00:26:30,759 --> 00:26:32,079
you need to take good care of your health.

486
00:26:33,119 --> 00:26:33,799
Thanks.

487
00:27:39,440 --> 00:27:40,799
Sponge cakes, fried dough sticks, tea eggs

488
00:27:41,079 --> 00:27:44,079
Sponge cakes, fried dough sticks, tea eggs

489
00:27:44,079 --> 00:27:44,680
Two mao

490
00:27:53,720 --> 00:27:54,880
Everyone says you're leaving.

491
00:27:55,000 --> 00:27:56,880
Xiao Lei from Division 3 was asking me today.

492
00:27:57,319 --> 00:27:59,279
He said your paperwork is at the final step.

493
00:28:00,279 --> 00:28:01,400
What are your thoughts?

494
00:28:02,519 --> 00:28:04,319
I can still work for here from the outside.

495
00:28:04,319 --> 00:28:04,920
It's all the same.

496
00:28:08,400 --> 00:28:09,480
Are you really planning to leave?

497
00:28:11,599 --> 00:28:12,279
That's classified.

498
00:28:13,440 --> 00:28:14,640
That guy you caught yesterday...

499
00:28:14,839 --> 00:28:16,279
He doesn't seem to be very high-ranking.

500
00:28:16,480 --> 00:28:17,359
Our Division 2...

501
00:28:17,480 --> 00:28:19,200
We even mobilized thermoses and mops.

502
00:28:19,440 --> 00:28:20,319
All that fuss for nothing.

503
00:28:21,480 --> 00:28:22,640
It wasn't exactly for nothing.

504
00:28:22,960 --> 00:28:24,400
It just feels, how should I put it...

505
00:28:24,839 --> 00:28:26,079
Like shooting a mosquito with a cannon.

506
00:28:26,079 --> 00:28:26,640
Exactly.

507
00:28:26,640 --> 00:28:28,000
Shooting a mosquito with a cannon.

508
00:28:28,319 --> 00:28:29,400
Alright, alright.

509
00:28:29,519 --> 00:28:30,920
At least you guys get to run around.

510
00:28:31,160 --> 00:28:33,200
We have to review files every day.

511
00:28:33,319 --> 00:28:34,680
Surviving purely on coffee.

512
00:28:34,960 --> 00:28:36,319
Reviewing from morning until dawn.

513
00:28:36,480 --> 00:28:38,079
My eyes are going blind from all the reading.

514
00:28:38,680 --> 00:28:39,680
That coffee of yours...

515
00:28:39,680 --> 00:28:41,400
You're better off drinking nutritious milk.

516
00:28:41,400 --> 00:28:43,000
I thought we'd get to carry guns.

517
00:28:43,119 --> 00:28:44,119
But when I asked right before leaving...

518
00:28:44,119 --> 00:28:45,400
We didn't even get batons.

519
00:28:45,400 --> 00:28:47,000
I was even hoping for bulletproof vests.

520
00:28:48,000 --> 00:28:49,559
Long pants and sleeves are still necessary.

521
00:28:49,559 --> 00:28:50,640
If you happen to scrape the ground,

522
00:28:50,640 --> 00:28:52,400
you could easily skin your arms and legs.

523
00:28:53,039 --> 00:28:53,880
It was just a small fry.

524
00:28:53,920 --> 00:28:55,920
You and Brother Qi could've handled him.

525
00:28:56,119 --> 00:28:57,799
Why use a sledgehammer to crack a nut?

526
00:29:00,200 --> 00:29:01,200
It really wasn't satisfying.

527
00:29:01,759 --> 00:29:02,880
Before I even realized what was happening,

528
00:29:02,880 --> 00:29:03,799
the guy was already caught.

529
00:29:03,839 --> 00:29:05,680
When will we get to work on a big case?

530
00:29:05,759 --> 00:29:07,160
You'll just have to wait for a big case.

531
00:29:07,160 --> 00:29:08,039
Director Wu.

532
00:29:10,759 --> 00:29:11,079
Director Wu.

533
00:29:11,240 --> 00:29:11,599
Director Wu.

534
00:29:11,799 --> 00:29:12,480
Director Wu.

535
00:29:18,759 --> 00:29:19,599
Just a reminder.

536
00:29:19,920 --> 00:29:20,880
Those of us in intelligence work

537
00:29:21,319 --> 00:29:23,160
should habitually lower our voices

538
00:29:23,559 --> 00:29:24,440
by an octave,

539
00:29:24,720 --> 00:29:25,640
anywhere we go.

540
00:29:26,279 --> 00:29:26,799
Unless...

541
00:29:27,960 --> 00:29:28,880
you want to give a speech.

542
00:29:30,240 --> 00:29:30,920
Have a seat.

543
00:29:38,079 --> 00:29:39,559
Like using a marble slab to press a pickle jar.

544
00:29:39,680 --> 00:29:40,519
You all must feel underutilized.

545
00:29:43,960 --> 00:29:44,960
What counts as a big case?

546
00:29:45,240 --> 00:29:46,039
How many people must be arrested?

547
00:29:46,559 --> 00:29:47,200
How many buildings blown up?

548
00:29:47,960 --> 00:29:48,759
How many cars crashed?

549
00:29:49,119 --> 00:29:50,400
How much of the state's money must be spent

550
00:29:50,880 --> 00:29:51,880
for it to count as a big case?

551
00:29:58,880 --> 00:29:59,519
You...

552
00:30:02,240 --> 00:30:03,720
Minor intel is beneath you, isn't it?

553
00:30:04,240 --> 00:30:04,759
I'll tell you what.

554
00:30:05,119 --> 00:30:06,119
In one week's time,

555
00:30:06,440 --> 00:30:07,400
gather all the world's

556
00:30:07,759 --> 00:30:09,000
nuclear submarine blueprints

557
00:30:09,000 --> 00:30:09,920
and put them on my desk.

558
00:30:11,160 --> 00:30:12,000
Earth-shattering, isn't it?

559
00:30:13,440 --> 00:30:14,319
Doing intelligence work,

560
00:30:14,759 --> 00:30:16,200
you have to shock Taiwan, China first,

561
00:30:16,519 --> 00:30:17,599
then scare the Americans

562
00:30:17,680 --> 00:30:19,319
into wetting their pants and shoes.

563
00:30:19,960 --> 00:30:20,680
Pretty impressive, right?

564
00:30:21,519 --> 00:30:22,359
A real moment of glory!

565
00:30:29,200 --> 00:30:29,839
Catching spies.

566
00:30:30,359 --> 00:30:31,160
You want to be issued guns.

567
00:30:33,839 --> 00:30:34,559
Submachine guns, even.

568
00:30:34,839 --> 00:30:36,839
And catch dozens of spies at once.

569
00:30:37,440 --> 00:30:38,279
Have you ever considered,

570
00:30:38,839 --> 00:30:39,960
if there really were such an operation,

571
00:30:41,039 --> 00:30:42,079
how many enemies would die?

572
00:30:43,640 --> 00:30:44,519
How many of our comrades

573
00:30:45,799 --> 00:30:46,960
might have to sacrifice their lives?

574
00:30:49,880 --> 00:30:51,400
If there really were such a big case,

575
00:30:52,519 --> 00:30:53,240
behind it,

576
00:30:54,079 --> 00:30:55,440
how many state secrets would have been leaked?

577
00:30:55,920 --> 00:30:56,960
How many people would face the firing squad?

578
00:30:58,799 --> 00:30:59,720
How many children

579
00:31:00,440 --> 00:31:01,480
would wake up in the morning

580
00:31:02,240 --> 00:31:03,160
to find their parents gone?

581
00:31:03,799 --> 00:31:05,400
And how many white-haired elders,

582
00:31:06,880 --> 00:31:07,759
in a single day,

583
00:31:08,839 --> 00:31:09,799
would lose

584
00:31:09,799 --> 00:31:11,640
the sons meant to care for them in their old age?

585
00:31:13,079 --> 00:31:13,880
Answer me.

586
00:31:19,960 --> 00:31:21,240
On the hidden front...

587
00:31:21,240 --> 00:31:22,279
think it through before you speak.

588
00:31:22,680 --> 00:31:23,720
Go to my office after you eat.

589
00:31:25,599 --> 00:31:26,519
Once you've thought it through,

590
00:31:26,680 --> 00:31:27,480
come and tell me.

591
00:31:36,400 --> 00:31:37,400
Fickle.

592
00:31:37,680 --> 00:31:38,680
Shifting loyalties.

593
00:31:39,039 --> 00:31:40,680
Still restless after your transfer.

594
00:31:41,079 --> 00:31:42,200
Wanting to leave when you're in the bureau,

595
00:31:43,039 --> 00:31:44,240
and wanting to come back once you're out.

596
00:31:44,319 --> 00:31:46,279
Nobody knows what you really want to do.

597
00:31:49,240 --> 00:31:50,119
In intelligence work,

598
00:31:51,559 --> 00:31:52,839
you must blend truth and fiction.

599
00:31:53,200 --> 00:31:54,359
Everyone in the bureau now knows

600
00:31:54,359 --> 00:31:55,519
your affiliation is with Section 1.

601
00:31:56,319 --> 00:31:57,759
But in reality, your true superior

602
00:31:58,240 --> 00:31:59,119
is Section Chief Wei.

603
00:31:59,319 --> 00:32:00,079
Whether it's a secondment,

604
00:32:00,319 --> 00:32:01,160
or just rumors,

605
00:32:01,599 --> 00:32:02,480
they're all smokescreens.

606
00:32:03,000 --> 00:32:03,759
From now on,

607
00:32:04,119 --> 00:32:05,839
no matter the lie, you can cover it up,

608
00:32:06,279 --> 00:32:07,279
and make it plausible.

609
00:32:09,680 --> 00:32:11,759
Chief Wei thinks I'm suited to be a tour guide.

610
00:32:12,400 --> 00:32:14,240
Am I really guiding a tour to Wuyi Mountain?

611
00:32:15,640 --> 00:32:16,720
Being a tour guide is great.

612
00:32:17,079 --> 00:32:18,039
You can go anywhere.

613
00:32:19,079 --> 00:32:20,240
If I were 30 years younger,

614
00:32:20,720 --> 00:32:22,119
I'd jump at the chance to do this job.

615
00:32:23,759 --> 00:32:24,920
You can visit Wuyi Mountain,

616
00:32:25,319 --> 00:32:26,440
and Gulangyu too.

617
00:32:27,200 --> 00:32:29,119
I have zero experience in intelligence work.

618
00:32:29,480 --> 00:32:30,640
Why was I chosen?

619
00:32:31,160 --> 00:32:32,920
Section Chief Wei's report stated that,

620
00:32:34,079 --> 00:32:35,680
among your batch of new recruits,

621
00:32:36,000 --> 00:32:36,839
relatively speaking,

622
00:32:37,200 --> 00:32:37,880
you are outstanding,

623
00:32:38,480 --> 00:32:39,279
and quite unique.

624
00:32:40,119 --> 00:32:41,079
You also have a gender advantage.

625
00:32:41,519 --> 00:32:42,519
Most importantly,

626
00:32:44,039 --> 00:32:44,920
intelligence work

627
00:32:45,599 --> 00:32:46,599
requires talent.

628
00:32:49,880 --> 00:32:50,799
What is your name?

629
00:32:51,359 --> 00:32:52,279
Yu Lixia.

630
00:32:53,160 --> 00:32:54,039
Letting it go to your head?

631
00:32:57,960 --> 00:32:58,839
Always remember,

632
00:32:58,839 --> 00:32:59,799
your name is Jin Lan.

633
00:33:00,359 --> 00:33:02,720
You must completely forget the name Yu Lixia.

634
00:33:02,880 --> 00:33:04,039
Starting today,

635
00:33:04,119 --> 00:33:05,279
you must do your best to cut off

636
00:33:05,279 --> 00:33:06,960
contact with your friends and classmates.

637
00:33:07,240 --> 00:33:08,440
Every task in the bureau,

638
00:33:08,480 --> 00:33:09,200
every single matter,

639
00:33:09,440 --> 00:33:10,799
must be kept secret from everyone.

640
00:33:11,799 --> 00:33:12,839
Do you know why?

641
00:33:13,920 --> 00:33:15,000
Because of organizational discipline.

642
00:33:15,519 --> 00:33:16,759
Because intelligence work

643
00:33:17,880 --> 00:33:19,039
involves turned assets.

644
00:33:20,079 --> 00:33:20,960
If there's a leak,

645
00:33:21,480 --> 00:33:23,160
they could lose their heads.

646
00:33:23,880 --> 00:33:25,039
A single sentence from you,

647
00:33:25,519 --> 00:33:26,920
or even a single word,

648
00:33:27,519 --> 00:33:29,160
could mean a living, breathing life.

649
00:33:31,359 --> 00:33:32,359
Perhaps one day,

650
00:33:32,759 --> 00:33:33,759
a suitable friend,

651
00:33:34,359 --> 00:33:35,839
someone you need to befriend,

652
00:33:36,240 --> 00:33:37,119
will fall right into your lap.

653
00:33:38,200 --> 00:33:39,079
When that day comes,

654
00:33:39,599 --> 00:33:40,599
that will be the time you resign,

655
00:33:41,079 --> 00:33:42,279
or transfer out.

656
00:33:43,279 --> 00:33:44,079
A friend?

657
00:33:45,640 --> 00:33:46,359
How do I make this friend?

658
00:33:46,880 --> 00:33:47,920
When will they come?

659
00:33:48,079 --> 00:33:48,680
You wait.

660
00:33:49,759 --> 00:33:51,119
In intelligence work,

661
00:33:51,160 --> 00:33:53,440
the most important thing is waiting patiently.

662
00:33:55,200 --> 00:33:56,279
Anything else to add?

663
00:34:06,960 --> 00:34:08,000
I didn't have lunch.

664
00:34:08,000 --> 00:34:09,159
I'm running on empty.

665
00:34:09,159 --> 00:34:10,400
You said you've seen this man.

666
00:34:10,400 --> 00:34:10,880
When?

667
00:34:10,880 --> 00:34:11,639
Where?

668
00:34:11,840 --> 00:34:13,039
Before the training course.

669
00:34:13,239 --> 00:34:14,239
He delivered a package to me.

670
00:34:14,239 --> 00:34:15,400
Why didn't you go after him when he ran?

671
00:34:15,840 --> 00:34:17,559
I was caught off guard.

672
00:34:17,559 --> 00:34:19,000
I didn't expect him to come out.

673
00:34:19,079 --> 00:34:20,079
If I were your superior,

674
00:34:20,679 --> 00:34:21,719
I would suspect you.

675
00:34:22,760 --> 00:34:25,519
I think He Chunxiao is suspicious.

676
00:34:39,519 --> 00:34:40,480
Whatever you do,

677
00:34:40,880 --> 00:34:41,480
whatever you do,

678
00:34:41,480 --> 00:34:42,400
do not baselessly suspect

679
00:34:42,400 --> 00:34:43,920
your own comrades and brothers in arms.

680
00:34:45,119 --> 00:34:45,719
Unless

681
00:34:46,800 --> 00:34:48,320
you have ironclad evidence.

682
00:35:03,360 --> 00:35:03,920
You missed something.

683
00:35:05,559 --> 00:35:06,360
Missed what?

684
00:35:07,480 --> 00:35:08,960
You left out four details.

685
00:35:09,280 --> 00:35:10,039
Which parts did I miss?

686
00:35:10,039 --> 00:35:10,639
Figure it out yourself.

687
00:35:14,440 --> 00:35:15,800
Was it at the textile mill?

688
00:35:16,199 --> 00:35:17,559
Where we met my brother-in-law?

689
00:35:19,920 --> 00:35:20,880
Are you asking me?

690
00:35:23,360 --> 00:35:24,679
We said so much today,

691
00:35:24,679 --> 00:35:25,880
and went to so many places.

692
00:35:26,719 --> 00:35:27,960
Can you really remember it all?

693
00:35:28,320 --> 00:35:29,760
Would I be testing you if I couldn't?

694
00:35:30,960 --> 00:35:32,760
From the first second you opened your eyes,

695
00:35:32,760 --> 00:35:33,679
think carefully.

696
00:35:33,679 --> 00:35:35,280
One mistake, you buy me dinner.

697
00:35:35,280 --> 00:35:36,039
Two mistakes,

698
00:35:36,239 --> 00:35:37,320
you run laps around the track.

699
00:35:37,360 --> 00:35:38,039
Three mistakes,

700
00:35:38,559 --> 00:35:39,159
you're out.

701
00:35:52,840 --> 00:35:53,800
What are you doing here?

702
00:35:54,639 --> 00:35:55,719
My uncle lives around here.

703
00:35:55,719 --> 00:35:56,360
I came to visit.

704
00:35:56,639 --> 00:35:57,159
What about you?

705
00:35:57,400 --> 00:35:58,320
I'm looking for someone.

706
00:35:58,480 --> 00:35:59,559
It's your brother-in-law.

707
00:35:59,719 --> 00:36:01,400
He insisted on showing me some textile mill.

708
00:36:01,920 --> 00:36:02,920
It's about to go under.

709
00:36:25,079 --> 00:36:25,760
Who's this?

710
00:36:26,119 --> 00:36:27,039
It's me, brother-in-law.

711
00:36:27,400 --> 00:36:29,239
My sister says you're at the office every day.

712
00:36:29,639 --> 00:36:30,639
Why aren't you home yet?

713
00:36:30,760 --> 00:36:31,760
I'm working overtime.

714
00:36:32,039 --> 00:36:32,880
What's up? Do you need something?

715
00:36:33,480 --> 00:36:34,400
The thing is...

716
00:36:35,280 --> 00:36:37,559
Is that textile factory about to go under?

717
00:36:37,840 --> 00:36:39,559
I saw you visiting the factory the other day.

718
00:36:39,840 --> 00:36:41,039
Are they planning a buyout?

719
00:36:41,519 --> 00:36:42,760
How would I know?

720
00:36:43,039 --> 00:36:43,800
What are you getting at?

721
00:36:44,679 --> 00:36:45,800
He might not invest,

722
00:36:46,000 --> 00:36:46,960
but you still showed him around.

723
00:36:47,159 --> 00:36:49,159
Isn't that just how you guys do business?

724
00:36:49,360 --> 00:36:51,440
You cast your net whether there's fish or not, right?

725
00:36:52,639 --> 00:36:54,000
Here's the thing, brother-in-law.

726
00:36:54,000 --> 00:36:55,639
My uncle's kid...

727
00:36:55,840 --> 00:36:58,079
You met him at my place for New Year's.

728
00:36:58,119 --> 00:37:00,320
The one who's taller than me.

729
00:37:00,360 --> 00:37:01,719
He's been sitting around at home lately.

730
00:37:02,039 --> 00:37:03,519
If that Lin Kanshan

731
00:37:03,679 --> 00:37:04,880
really acquires the textile factory,

732
00:37:05,079 --> 00:37:06,400
I was thinking,

733
00:37:06,639 --> 00:37:08,199
could you get him a job there?

734
00:37:08,760 --> 00:37:11,280
Wait for the deal to close before giving out jobs.

735
00:37:11,519 --> 00:37:12,519
Anything else?

736
00:37:13,159 --> 00:37:15,239
I've been showing the investors from Taiwan, China around.

737
00:37:15,280 --> 00:37:17,079
These guys are real workaholics.

738
00:37:17,119 --> 00:37:18,880
Looking around everywhere every day.

739
00:37:19,079 --> 00:37:20,920
If that's all, I'm going to hang up.

740
00:37:20,920 --> 00:37:21,840
I'm really busy right now.

741
00:37:22,000 --> 00:37:22,679
Alright, brother-in-law.

742
00:37:22,880 --> 00:37:23,400
Okay.

743
00:37:44,079 --> 00:37:46,360
Investigate the latest naval port deployments

744
00:37:46,559 --> 00:37:48,000
and details of recent exercises.

745
00:37:48,159 --> 00:37:49,000
Report back immediately.

746
00:38:36,199 --> 00:38:36,800
What are you doing?

747
00:38:43,039 --> 00:38:44,079
Do you know where you are?

748
00:38:44,440 --> 00:38:45,920
You're filming a naval pier.

749
00:38:46,440 --> 00:38:48,039
Defense facilities are highly classified.

750
00:38:48,159 --> 00:38:50,039
Leaking info can get you arrested and jailed.

751
00:38:50,599 --> 00:38:51,079
Hand it over.

752
00:38:55,440 --> 00:38:55,920
Don't move.

753
00:39:02,199 --> 00:39:02,679
Beat it.

754
00:39:09,159 --> 00:39:10,039
Section Chief Wei.

755
00:39:10,280 --> 00:39:11,639
I'd like to request a new partner.

756
00:39:12,199 --> 00:39:13,280
What's wrong with Hua Dong?

757
00:39:13,280 --> 00:39:15,840
He Chunxiao complements me better.

758
00:39:16,239 --> 00:39:18,400
Changing partners is like dating.

759
00:39:18,400 --> 00:39:20,519
How do I know who fits better without spending time?

760
00:39:20,960 --> 00:39:22,400
It's not a blind date. You don't have to commit.

761
00:39:22,480 --> 00:39:23,719
What's the harm in switching?

762
00:39:23,840 --> 00:39:24,719
You said it.

763
00:39:26,239 --> 00:39:27,960
So, do you mean this is temporary...

764
00:39:28,000 --> 00:39:29,079
...or permanent?

765
00:39:34,360 --> 00:39:36,199
We have an operation today anyway.

766
00:39:36,320 --> 00:39:37,599
If it's a good fit, it'll be permanent.

767
00:39:37,599 --> 00:39:38,760
If not, it's temporary.

768
00:39:40,599 --> 00:39:41,239
All right.

769
00:39:49,880 --> 00:39:50,599
You're here.

770
00:39:51,280 --> 00:39:51,960
What'll it be?

771
00:39:52,079 --> 00:39:52,719
The usual.

772
00:39:53,360 --> 00:39:54,320
Got it, the usual.

773
00:39:55,199 --> 00:39:56,119
Here, your flatbread.

774
00:39:56,480 --> 00:39:57,239
And your porridge.

775
00:39:57,360 --> 00:39:58,079
Here you go.

776
00:39:58,360 --> 00:39:58,559
Take care.

777
00:39:58,559 --> 00:39:59,039
Thanks.

778
00:39:59,039 --> 00:39:59,800
You're welcome.

779
00:40:07,039 --> 00:40:09,360
Tailing is our magnifying glass.

780
00:40:09,480 --> 00:40:11,519
Observe the target's walking habits.

781
00:40:11,519 --> 00:40:13,280
Does he usually step with his left foot...

782
00:40:13,280 --> 00:40:14,239
...or his right foot?

783
00:40:14,239 --> 00:40:15,440
See if, while walking, he...

784
00:40:15,440 --> 00:40:16,840
...subconsciously touches his pockets.

785
00:40:16,840 --> 00:40:18,960
You also need to read the environment.

786
00:40:19,159 --> 00:40:20,559
Which shop's window...

787
00:40:20,679 --> 00:40:22,639
...can reflect the target's movements.

788
00:40:22,639 --> 00:40:23,239
Which intersection...

789
00:40:23,320 --> 00:40:24,960
...allows us to take cover quickly.

790
00:40:41,400 --> 00:40:42,639
Looking so eagerly,

791
00:40:43,360 --> 00:40:44,840
are you looking for me or a girlfriend?

792
00:40:45,719 --> 00:40:46,519
Have you ever been in love?

793
00:40:46,519 --> 00:40:47,159
What?

794
00:40:47,559 --> 00:40:48,880
Never chased a girl?

795
00:40:49,239 --> 00:40:50,280
It's the kind where in the whole world,

796
00:40:50,400 --> 00:40:51,840
you only have eyes for her.

797
00:40:51,840 --> 00:40:53,480
You can't see anyone else but her.

798
00:40:53,880 --> 00:40:54,559
Even if a thief

799
00:40:54,719 --> 00:40:56,519
reached into your pocket, you wouldn't notice.

800
00:40:56,880 --> 00:40:57,800
Just like right now.

801
00:40:59,559 --> 00:41:01,039
Tailing someone is the same.

802
00:41:01,920 --> 00:41:04,119
Total single-mind...

803
00:41:05,239 --> 00:41:05,960
How do you say that word again?

804
00:41:05,960 --> 00:41:06,559
Edness.

805
00:41:11,119 --> 00:41:13,039
I'll make your brain think about

806
00:41:13,039 --> 00:41:14,800
how to spell "single-mindedness".

807
00:41:14,800 --> 00:41:16,599
Once you're distracted, I can strike.

808
00:41:17,000 --> 00:41:18,719
Your anti-tracking awareness is zero.

809
00:41:19,280 --> 00:41:20,480
Why are you secretly following me?

810
00:41:20,840 --> 00:41:22,320
Apply what you learn. You said it.

811
00:41:22,320 --> 00:41:23,559
I wanted to try it out too.

812
00:41:23,599 --> 00:41:24,760
In future surveillance operations,

813
00:41:24,760 --> 00:41:26,320
how can I avoid being spotted?

814
00:41:26,480 --> 00:41:28,119
That depends on who you are monitoring.

815
00:41:28,239 --> 00:41:29,280
Tailing a second grader,

816
00:41:29,280 --> 00:41:30,320
you probably won't be exposed.

817
00:41:30,320 --> 00:41:31,880
A third grader is hard to say.

818
00:41:33,880 --> 00:41:34,559
Tell me.

819
00:41:34,880 --> 00:41:36,079
Who is the target on your mind?

820
00:41:36,400 --> 00:41:37,239
A businessman from Taiwan, China.

821
00:41:37,639 --> 00:41:38,559
In the nightclub restroom,

822
00:41:38,559 --> 00:41:39,960
the one who helped me out.

823
00:41:40,760 --> 00:41:41,599
Is there a problem?

824
00:41:42,119 --> 00:41:44,119
I saw him in the post office backyard.

825
00:41:44,719 --> 00:41:45,559
Theoretically speaking,

826
00:41:45,599 --> 00:41:47,199
his movement trajectory is suspicious.

827
00:41:47,360 --> 00:41:48,199
But I verified it.

828
00:41:48,280 --> 00:41:49,480
He does have a legitimate reason.

829
00:41:49,800 --> 00:41:51,119
So I can't really say.

830
00:41:51,719 --> 00:41:53,280
Think it through before you speak then.

831
00:41:53,320 --> 00:41:54,519
Focus on getting today's job done first.

832
00:41:55,400 --> 00:41:56,440
What's the job today?

833
00:41:58,800 --> 00:42:00,719
A huge op only young people can handle.

834
00:42:00,719 --> 00:42:01,679
Didn't anyone notify you?

835
00:42:06,599 --> 00:42:07,800
From the city center to Mawei,

836
00:42:08,199 --> 00:42:09,840
around the docks and near the schools,

837
00:42:09,840 --> 00:42:11,000
check the utility poles one by one.

838
00:42:11,000 --> 00:42:12,199
Look carefully at every single one.

839
00:42:12,400 --> 00:42:14,599
There are ads for photography enthusiasts,

840
00:42:14,599 --> 00:42:15,920
specifically to take pictures of the docks.

841
00:42:15,920 --> 00:42:17,199
Mailing addresses,

842
00:42:17,199 --> 00:42:18,280
pager numbers,

843
00:42:18,280 --> 00:42:19,920
and identity info must all be memorized.

844
00:42:19,920 --> 00:42:20,719
Track and investigate them one by one.

845
00:42:21,119 --> 00:42:22,679
The Taiwan Strait situation is escalating.

846
00:42:23,039 --> 00:42:24,920
The "Military Intelligence Bureau" is overreaching.

847
00:42:24,960 --> 00:42:27,039
Intel on the naval dock is a priority.

848
00:42:27,119 --> 00:42:27,920
We must catch the elephants,

849
00:42:27,920 --> 00:42:28,800
and the mosquitoes too.

850
00:42:28,800 --> 00:42:30,159
Today, we are here to catch mosquitoes.

851
00:42:30,559 --> 00:42:31,280
Two people per group.

852
00:42:31,280 --> 00:42:32,280
Divide and zone the areas.

853
00:42:32,880 --> 00:42:34,440
Upset that I swapped you out?

854
00:42:34,719 --> 00:42:35,719
Don't want to go out?

855
00:42:35,719 --> 00:42:37,760
Sitting in the office drinking tea is nice.

856
00:42:38,280 --> 00:42:39,079
No.

857
00:42:39,079 --> 00:42:41,159
Brother Qi made me recount everything that happens,

858
00:42:41,159 --> 00:42:41,800
every word spoken,

859
00:42:41,800 --> 00:42:42,400
every person met,

860
00:42:42,400 --> 00:42:44,519
and everything done, all clearly.

861
00:42:44,519 --> 00:42:45,519
He checks it every day.

862
00:42:45,519 --> 00:42:47,360
One more mistake and he'll drop me.

863
00:42:49,960 --> 00:42:51,360
He only knows how to make demands of others.

864
00:42:51,360 --> 00:42:52,639
Can he remember all that himself?

865
00:42:53,199 --> 00:42:54,079
He really can.

866
00:42:54,519 --> 00:42:55,519
I asked.

867
00:42:55,519 --> 00:42:57,320
I don't know if he has a trick,

868
00:42:57,320 --> 00:42:58,880
or if some just have a naturally good memory.

869
00:43:08,400 --> 00:43:09,119
I am Wang Kai.

870
00:43:09,480 --> 00:43:10,840
Inviting you to watch the TV drama

871
00:43:11,119 --> 00:43:11,840
Crossfire.

872
00:43:12,559 --> 00:43:14,800
Dried shrimp prices in the market were stable,

873
00:43:14,800 --> 00:43:15,719
but suddenly went up.

874
00:43:15,800 --> 00:43:16,480
The county hospital

875
00:43:16,480 --> 00:43:18,119
and Chengguan Town Hospital's heatstroke meds

876
00:43:18,119 --> 00:43:19,599
are selling much more than usual.

877
00:43:19,599 --> 00:43:21,039
This unit most likely

878
00:43:21,159 --> 00:43:23,559
is from the Beijing Military Region, unaccustomed to humidity.

879
00:43:23,800 --> 00:43:24,639
The people over there

880
00:43:24,639 --> 00:43:25,800
want to catch a big fish.

881
00:43:25,800 --> 00:43:26,559
How big?

882
00:43:26,719 --> 00:43:27,840
As big as a missile.

883
00:43:28,000 --> 00:43:30,039
The 761 Institute recently made a breakthrough

884
00:43:30,039 --> 00:43:30,800
in missile fuel.

885
00:43:30,880 --> 00:43:32,639
They are definitely coming for this.

886
00:43:32,679 --> 00:43:33,559
Something big is going to happen.

887
00:43:34,079 --> 00:43:34,840
Are you crazy!

888
00:43:35,239 --> 00:43:36,519
Why are you so nervous?
